ing a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be verified, restored quickly, and protected from the very threats it is meant to guard against (such as ransomware or hardware failure).\n\nHere is a detailed guide on designing a professional-grade backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Backup Strategies: Full vs. Incremental\nA reliable system rarely relies on a single method; it uses a hybrid approach to balance storage efficiency with recovery speed.\n\n#### Full Backups\nA full backup copies every selected", "elapsed_s": 3.691022756975144, "ttft_s": 0.542236645007506, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 182, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 54, "prompt_ms": 473.099, "prompt_per_token_ms": 8.761092592592592, "prompt_per_second": 114.14101488272011, "predicted_n": 128, "predicted_ms": 3148.096, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.78815748031496, "predicted_per_second": 40.341844721380795}, "finish_reason": "length", "decode_tps_client": 40.333003095163946, "end_to_end_output_tps": 34.678734981547, "full_output_budget": true}, "measured": [{"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system is not merely about copying data from one drive to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be restored. If the backup fails during a crisis, it is not a backup\u2014it is an archive.\n\nBelow is a comprehensive guide to designing a professional-grade file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Foundational Strategy: The 3-2-1 Rule\nBefore choosing tools, adhere to the industry standard for data redundancy:\n*   **3 Copies of Data:** Your primary data plus two backups.\n*   **2 Different Media", "elapsed_s": 3.688492765999399, "ttft_s": 0.5479860450141132, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 183, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 55, "prompt_ms": 472.56