tegy: The 3-2-1 Rule\nBefore choosing tools, adhere to the industry standard for data redundancy:\n*   **3 Copies of Data:** One primary copy and two backups.\n*   **2 Different Media Types:** (e", "elapsed_s": 3.686257049033884, "ttft_s": 0.5402766800252721, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 183, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 55, "prompt_ms": 471.211, "prompt_per_token_ms": 8.567472727272728, "prompt_per_second": 116.7205349620446, "predicted_n": 128, "predicted_ms": 3145.966, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.771385826771652, "predicted_per_second": 40.36915847151559}, "finish_reason": "length", "decode_tps_client": 40.36897408867854, "end_to_end_output_tps": 34.72356873038656, "full_output_budget": true}], "decode_tps_client_median": 40.369852042728425, "ttft_s_median": 0.5479860450141132, "pass": true, "distinct_output_texts": 3}, "long": {"tier": "development", "anchor": {"text": "BOLT-7319-CEDAR", "elapsed_s": 11.182213805965148, "ttft_s": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 11, "prompt_tokens": 8238, "total_tokens": 8249, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 8238, "prompt_ms": 10858.823, "prompt_per_token_ms": 1.3181382617140083, "prompt_per_second": 758.6457574637693, "predicted_n": 11, "predicted_ms": 256.533, "predicted_per_token_ms": 25.6533, "predicted_per_second": 38.98133963271781}, "finish_reason": "stop", "decode_tps_client": null, "end_to_end_output_tps": 0.9837050329096778, "full_output_budget": false}, "warmup": {"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system requires a shift in mindset from simply \"copying files\" to implementing a **data resilience strategy**. The goal is not just to have a copy of your data, but to ensure that copy is recoverable, secure, and independent of the primary system's failures.\n\nHere is a comprehensive guide to designing a reliable file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Cor